Magnetization measurements revealed ferromagnetic behavior with high Curie temperature. The alloy followed the Slater-Pauling rule reasonably well, indicating half-metallic nature.

Electrical resistivity measurements showed metallic behavior. At low temperature, localization behavior was observed due to scattering effects. The resistivity behavior can be expressed as:

\[
\rho(T) = \rho_0 + BT^n
\]

where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\rho(T)$ = electrical resistivity
    \item $\rho_0$ = residual resistivity
    \item $B$ = constant
    \item $n$ = temperature exponent
\end{itemize}

