The coexistence of half-metallic ferromagnetism and localized transport behavior makes CoRuMnSi an important material for future spintronic devices.

\section{Conclusion}

This review summarizes the important properties of CoRuMnSi Heusler alloy. The alloy showed ordered crystal structure, ferromagnetic behavior, and metallic electrical transport properties. The introduction of Ru reduced structural disorder and improved magnetic characteristics. Weak localization effects were observed at low temperature. Due to its half-metallic nature and good magnetic properties, CoRuMnSi is a promising candidate for spintronic applications.

